xmrswap end to end, all three exits, against REAL monerod and monero-wallet-rpc (regtest) and the DERO simulator
=============================================================================================================
Run 2026-09-11 16:45-17:24 AEST, tools/simhtlc built from the working tree (htlc.bas v2, the regtest fixes in
tools/xmrswap/monero.go and fakewallet.go). The raw driver output follows this header; machine paths are replaced
with <tmp>, <repo>, <user>.

What was real and what was not
- Monero: monerod 0.18.5.1-release, nettype fakechain (--regtest), http://127.0.0.1:28081, and two
  monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1 (alice http://127.0.0.1:28083, bob http://127.0.0.1:28084), all in WSL2, started per
  tools/regtest/README.md and not restarted. No fake wallet anywhere in this run: every Monero call went to the
  real servers, and every Monero txid below was looked up on the monerod (/get_transactions) and found in a block.
- DERO: the local DERO simulator (daemon 127.0.0.1:20000, wallets 127.0.0.1:30006 bob and 127.0.0.1:30007 alice).
  Not testnet, not mainnet. Both wallets' own histories (GetTransfers from height 570, read after the run) hold
  only this run's transactions, and nothing after them: no other process used them while it ran.
- Proofs: the real proof-xmr release build (the binary ProverSHA256 pins), run through wsl.exe; its self-test is
  at 38.2 s.
- Driver policy, not the companion's defaults: t1 = lock + 48, t2 = t1 + 8, G = 4, 10 Monero confirmations
  (one regtest block mined per round), stable 2, claim margin 2, close-after 3, Refund/Punish fee 2000.
  The companion's own defaults are t1 >= 400 blocks, G = 100, 20 confirmations, fee 3000.

Command (from <repo>/tools, built to simhtlc_e2e.exe):
  simhtlc -regtest -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the pinned proof-xmr release build>" -state-dir <tmp>/e2estate
  (every other flag at its default: -daemon 127.0.0.1:20000 -bob 127.0.0.1:30006 -alice 127.0.0.1:30007
   -monero-alice http://127.0.0.1:28083 -monero-bob http://127.0.0.1:28084 -monerod http://127.0.0.1:28081
   -paths happy,refund,punish -amount-dero 2000 -amount-xmr 1000000000000 -stipend 14016)
Result: exit 0; each exit ended with the contract holding 0 DERO.

