DERO accounting, from the wallets' own GetTransfers (fees included), matching the driver's balance line exactly
  bob   369931 -> 318952 = -50979: 3 locks x (2000 + fee 856) + 3 stipends x (14016 + fee 121) + refund fee 2000
        - the 2000 the refund returned
  alice 850583 -> 890020 = +39437: 3 stipends x 14016 + claim 2000 + punish 2000 - install fee 4107 - claim fee 504
        - punish fee 2000
  The stipend covered alice's whole gas in this run (504 + 2000 against 14016 each swap); the install is the
  driver's, not part of a swap.

What this run shows that the fake could not
- A view-only joint wallet made with generate_from_keys (no key check by the server; the client checked v.G and
  s.G against the address first) saw the real lock and counted it at 10 confirmations.
- The spend wallets built from s_a + s_b swept real outputs, and each sweep was confirmed from get_transfers
  out/pending before it was recorded, then found in a monerod block.
- Nothing in the run hit -50 (unlock_time), -4 (nothing unlocked) or an unsigned_txset.
- NOT shown by this run: set_daemon. simhtlc did not yet hand the companions a monerod (Config.Monerod was empty,
  so pinDaemon sent nothing), and the wallet-rpc used their own --daemon-address. Found while checking this
  header; run 2 below repeats all three exits with the monerod named, and counts what the server answered.

Not shown here: testnet or mainnet on either chain; an asset (U1) leg; a remote node; a crash mid-swap against the
real servers (the crash fuzz runs on the fake, which was reshaped to the real server's measured behaviour).

