RUN 3: htlc.bas v3, the same three exits, 2026-09-12 14:40-15:27 AEST
=============================================================================================================
tools/simhtlc -regtest, built from the working tree with xmrswap adapted to htlc.bas v3, before the fixes of the
review that followed. Those changed the maker's Reclaim path (reclaim_confirming) and the recovery card's wording,
not the happy, refund or punish logic run here. The driver installed its own htlc.bas v3 (scid 93f92162...,
code sha256 b785028da4a2554521d47f989f1011ec1f0a26be491e6a7eb2786c1f50834c36) with w1min 10, w2min 6, g2 30.
The prover was the reproducible proof-xmr build, sha256
7293e9c97e0330966499fff397a0488ef40d38f65da49423429c8c548c83d39d.
Real: monerod 0.18.5.1 --regtest (127.0.0.1:28081) and two monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1 (alice :28083, bob :28084)
in WSL2, and the DERO simulator (127.0.0.1:20000, wallets 30006 bob and 30007 alice). No fake wallet.

Outcomes (a Monero txid with a block number was found in that monerod block by the driver):
- happy:  alice claimed the DERO (38255f22..., stable at height 965); bob read s_a from the chain and swept the
          XMR (18e9e3e9..., monerod block 7128).
- refund: bob refunded (f120fe2f...); alice read s_b and swept her XMR back (fbf6c461..., monerod block 7824).
- punish: alice punished inside [t2, t2 + g2) (cb850e6b..., stable at height 1086); her XMR stays under the joint
          key, by design.
The contract held 0 DERO after every exit. DERO balances: bob 363929 -> 312944, alice 804805 -> 842980.
Not run live: v3's fourth exit, the maker's Reclaim, for which simhtlc has no path. It is covered by the DVM
suite (tests/htlc_v3_test.go) and by xmrswap's unit tests and crash fuzz.
Machine paths are replaced with <tmp>. The raw driver output follows.

