RUN 4: htlc.bas v3, all four exits, the maker's Reclaim included, 2026-09-12 17:32-19:08 AEST
=============================================================================================================
tools/simhtlc -regtest -paths happy,refund,punish,reclaim, built from the working tree (base e06c28a) with MT-B27
(the maker sends no Refund from t2 − 11 and counts it only once stable, phase refund_confirming), MT-B28 (the maker's
recovery card before his Lock, with wakes before t1 and t2 + g2) and simhtlc's new reclaim path. simhtlc's -t2 now
defaults to 20 blocks (it was 8, which the refund cutoff would leave no height to refund at). xmrswap's unit tests and
its crash fuzz (three passes) were green on this code. One change was made after the run, to wording only: beside the
last height each companion sends at, the recovery cards said "(t2 − 11)" and "(t2 + g2 − 21)", which are the cutoffs;
they now say t2 − 12 and t2 + g2 − 22, the heights printed. The heights printed below were already the right ones.
The driver installed its own htlc.bas v3 (scid e9d4ce0b..., code sha256
b785028da4a2554521d47f989f1011ec1f0a26be491e6a7eb2786c1f50834c36) with w1min 10, w2min 6, g2 30. The prover was the
reproducible proof-xmr build, sha256 7293e9c97e0330966499fff397a0488ef40d38f65da49423429c8c548c83d39d (1,340,640
bytes), checked before the run.
Real: monerod 0.18.5.1 --regtest (127.0.0.1:28081) and two monero-wallet-rpc 0.18.5.1 (alice :28083, bob :28084)
in WSL2, and the DERO simulator (127.0.0.1:20000, wallets 30006 bob and 30007 alice). No fake wallet. The driver
gives the companions no OS wake hook, so each card says that no wake was registered.
An earlier attempt at this run, started at 16:05, was stopped by the coordinator partway through its refund path, and
is not logged. It left one lock open on its own scratch install, recorded nowhere: scid c3dafa2b..., lock 1, 2,000
atomic units, t2 1344, t2 + g2 1374. That swap's taker locked regtest XMR at its joint address; only that maker's
Reclaim can close the lock, and it was left open.

Outcomes. A DERO txid's topoheight is what derod's DERO.GetTransaction reports as block_height; on the simulator it
is the height. A Monero txid with a block number was found in that monerod block by the driver.
- happy:   lock 0894bd98... (topoheight 1516) and stipend 92097336... (1526). Alice locked XMR (db214a79..., monerod
           block 9415) and claimed the DERO (bc63cd91..., topoheight 1546, stable at 1548). Bob read s_a from the
           chain and swept the XMR (6024fc4c..., monerod block 9507).
- refund:  lock 3bdb977e... (1562) and stipend 26a813b3... (1572). Alice locked XMR (91d6b4ee..., monerod block 9628).
           Bob came back at height 1610 (t1 1609) and refunded (3f3d9534..., topoheight 1611), before his refund
           cutoff 1618 (t2 1629 − 11). He counted the Refund only once it was stable (stable height 1612). Alice read
           s_b and swept her XMR back (e6be4b19..., monerod block 9853).
- punish:  lock a4f7e3a8... (1627) and stipend 2cc7604c... (1637). Alice locked XMR (9fc947fd..., monerod block
           10015). Bob vanished. Alice punished inside [t2 1694, t2 + g2 1724) (7ff57099..., topoheight 1695, stable
           at 1696). Bob sent no Punish of his own. Her XMR stays under the joint key, by design.
- reclaim: lock 0aefabc4... (topoheight 1711) and stipend 8b40cfbc... (1721). Alice locked XMR (9f42dfb8..., monerod
           block 10613); her companion was then stopped at height 1753 in await_refund, before t2 1777. Bob came back
           at 1766, his refund cutoff (t2 − 11), sent no Refund, and waited out the Punish window [1777, 1807), in
           which nobody punished. He Reclaimed from t2 + g2 = 1807 (912d99f8..., topoheight 1808) and counted it only
           once stable (stable height 1810). The chain then showed st_3 = 4 and sha256(xb_3) = hb_3. Alice's
           companion, restarted from its state file at 1807, sent no Punish, read s_b from xb_3 and swept her XMR
           back from the joint wallet (421a70b0..., monerod block 11197). This is the first live run of the Reclaim.
